      "writtenOn": "2026-07-15T05:54:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the new revision BejMacroSpec::marker is a std::string_view\ninstead of a char, and findMacroSpec() matches the marker as text with\nlongest-match, so the single-character assumption is gone: a multi-symbol marker\nlike %PD could be recognized and disambiguated from a single-char prefix.\n \nI\u0027m not adding those markers in this change, and to be clear the table only removes the identification limit -- each new marker still needs its own arity and\ninvalid-form handling to parse its operands. Verified by the existing unit tests\nfor %L/%I/%T/%C/%S.",
      "parentUuid": "da89a211_78e57884",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 253,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 253,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "f3d0dd12ec4d9d74b0a2e3d951b3cb831df3b7a8",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
